{"title":"2005 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Quick)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Quick)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For real numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, define <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/1/a81f1b7e7b46435693a5732cbe8c7c087c4d9c56.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a \\diamond b = \\sqrt{a^2 + b^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"130\" height=\"21\" />. What is the value of\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/5/79522e840b9fdb719bac0797215b14c7a7292ca4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(5 \\diamond 12) \\diamond ((-12) \\diamond (-5))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"189\" height=\"18\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/d/0ad4803b2fbbaf042f6fa9f1478376144abd89f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } 0 \\qquad \\textbf{(B) } \\frac{17}{2} \\qquad \\textbf{(C) } 13 \\qquad \\textbf{(D) } 13\\sqrt{2} \\qquad \\textbf{(E) } 26$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"420\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/4/a44772b24833895e84c5a4520c7e746a11556da6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} (5 \\diamond 12) \\diamond ((-12) \\diamond (-5))&amp;=(\\sqrt{5^2+12^2}) \\diamond (\\sqrt{(-12)^2+(-5)^2})\\\\ &amp;=(\\sqrt{169})\\diamond(\\sqrt{169})\\\\ &amp;=13\\diamond13\\\\  &amp;=\\sqrt{13^2+13^2}\\\\  &amp;=\\sqrt{338}\\\\  &amp;=\\boxed{\\mathrm{(D)\\,13\\sqrt{2}}}\\\\ \\end{align*}\" width=\"476\" height=\"186\" />\nNote that the negative signs did not matter and any number squared times two is that number times the square root of 2.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Quick.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Quick)\">Solution 2 (Quick)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Quick)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Notice that the formula given is for the hypotenuse of any right triangle. As stated in the first solution, the negative signs did not matter. Therefore, we can think of this in terms of right triangles. Knowing the 5-12-13 Pythagorean triple, we find it to be simplified to\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/8/698da55f751c20f3d0012b3251619d82706d16a8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(13 \\diamond 13)\\]\" width=\"64\" height=\"18\" />\nThen, knowing the 45-45-90 degree triangle ratio, we find the answer to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/9/249d8f358d966f7293e9a7598489b1e90a4a0aa0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[{(D)}\\]\" width=\"26\" height=\"18\" />\n~Thyauraisoverwhelming\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B\" title=\"2005 AMC 10B\">2005 AMC 10B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2005 AMC 10B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2005 AMC 10B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2005 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" ali